 m)","building_count":511,"extent_type":"Small Settlement Area","grid3_extent_id":"34NDG5753_1","adm1_pcode":"CD41","adm2_pcode":"CD4107","adm3_pcode":"CD410702","health_zone":"Djombo","health_area":"Ebongo Mbulu","name_source":"grid3_names:inside","assessments":[0]}},"assessments":[{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Djombo secteur villages (Djombo health zone: Djombo, Boso Ngwanza, Bobambo, Bosongo, Boso Maswa, Kodoro areas)","evidence":"Searches (FR/EN, 2025-2026) found no reports of armed groups, militias or rebel activity in Basankusu territory; conflict records for Basankusu and Djombo date from the 1999-2002 war (MLC vs FAC). The territory is remote forest in Equateur, far from eastern conflict zones and the Mobondo area; state authority via territorial administration and PNC is assumed. Djombo/Kodoro saw MLC abuses in 2000 but no recent armed activity is reported.","unit":"CD4107-basankusu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[32,33]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Basankusu secteur villages (Lisafa, Ndeke, Ilodze, Bongilima, Nsongo Nkoy, Bokakata, Lilangi, Monzonzo health areas)","evidence":"Searches (FR/EN, 2025-2026) found no reports of armed groups, militias or rebel activity in Basankusu territory; conflict records for Basankusu and Djombo date from the 1999-2002 war (MLC vs FAC). The territory is remote forest in Equateur, far from eastern conflict zones and the Mobondo area; state authority via territorial administration and PNC is assumed. Police presence in remote villages is thin; customary chiefs handle most disputes.","unit":"CD4107-basankusu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[31,32]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Basankusu town (territorial seat, river port at Lulonga/Maringa/Lopori confluence) and adjacent Ikau","evidence":"Basankusu is the territorial headquarters with territorial administration, PNC commissariat and a small FARDC presence. Searches (FR/EN, 2025-2026) found no reports of armed groups, militias or rebel activity in Basankusu territory; conflict records for Basankusu and Djombo date from the 1999-2002 war (MLC vs FAC). The territory is remote forest in Equateur, far from eastern conflict zones and the Mobondo area; state authority via territorial administration and PNC is assumed.","unit":"CD4107-basankusu","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[31,32]}],"sources":{"32":{"url":"https://strauss.tacc.utexas.edu/ccaps/armedConflictLocation/show/5523064","title":"CCAPS armed conflict location record (Basankusu, 1999-2000)","publisher":"Strauss Center CCAPS"},"33":{"url":"https://www.globalsecurity.org/military/library/news/2000/11/war-001103-afcod3.htm","title":"MLC atrocities near Basankusu, Djombo and Kodoro (2000)","publisher":"IRIN via GlobalSecurity","date":"2000-11-03"},"31":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basankusu","title":"Basankusu","publisher":"Wikipedia"}},"units":{"CD4107-basankusu":"Basankusu territory (Equateur) is a remote forested territory on the Lulonga/Maringa/Lopori rivers with no reported armed-group presence as of late 2026. Armed conflict records for Basankusu and Djombo date from the 1999-2002 war, when the MLC took the area. The state controls the territory through the territorial administration and the PNC, with a small FARDC presence in Basankusu town. All locations in the Basankusu and Djombo secteurs are assessed as default PNC control, with low confidence for rural villages."}}